   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x \\) and \\( dv = \\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\), so \\( du = dx \\) and \\( v = \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Tan",
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} - \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Sqrt",
                  3
               ],
               "Pi"
            ],
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral is \\( \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx = \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Ln",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{3} - \\left(\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\right) = - \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{3} \\).",
